emerhub.bali|https://www.instagram.com/p/DVLfWvCktHl/|2026-02-25|carousel|5|Operating Villa in Bali? \uc0\u55356 \u57309 \u65039 \\n\\nNew STR regulations are tightening across zoning, licensing, and OTA compliance.\\n\\nAuthorities are increasing supervision on PT PMA structures, KBLI classifications, OSS RBA registration, and short term rental listings on platforms like Airbnb and Booking.com. If your business activity does not align with your registered NIB, zoning designation, or licensing structure, you may face higher regulatory scrutiny, verification requests, or administrative review.\\n\\nThis is not a ban on villa operations but compliance standards in Bali are becoming more structured and actively monitored. Reviewing your business setup early helps prevent operational disruption as enforcement increases in 2026.\\n\\nAt Emerhub, we assist villa owners and investors in aligning their corporate structure with current Indonesian regulations.\\n\\n\u55357 \u56524  Save this post if you operate a villa in Bali\\n\u55357 \u56492  Unsure whether your structure is compliant? Send us a message\\n\\n#BaliVilla #STRBali #VillaCompliance #PTPMA #OSSIndonesia|#BaliVilla #STRBali #VillaCompliance #PTPMA #OSSIndonesia|Operating Villa in Bali? \u55356 \u57309 \u65039 |hidden|2||19:39|fonte=dom ; like_count hidden (ikon tanpa angka) ; bahasa=en\
